Drill 10 — Customer Cohort Retention by First-Seen Month
Exact task statement
Create customer cohorts by first-seen month and track how many customers and how much revenue remain active after 3, 6, and 12 months.
Build order
37.	Assign cohort_month as first_seen_month.
38.	Calculate cohort_size.
39.	Track active customers and cohort revenue at M0, M3, M6, and M12.
40.	Calculate customer and revenue retention percentages.
Validation checks
•	M0 active customers must equal cohort size.
•	Retention percentages must not exceed 100 percent.
•	Immature cohorts should have null M12 values rather than zero.
Final output template
cohort_month	cohort_size	m0_active_customers	m3_active_customers	m6_active_customers	m12_active_customers	m0_revenue	m3_revenue	m6_revenue	m12_revenue	customer_retention_pct_m12	revenue_retention_pct_m12
2025-01-01	42	42	31	28	24	6200000	5700000	5100000	4800000	57.1%	77.4%
Output column definitions
•	customer_retention_pct_m12 = m12_active_customers / cohort_size.
•	revenue_retention_pct_m12 = m12_revenue / m0_revenue.
•	Cohort month means the first month a customer appears in the dataset.

--======================================================================================================================
With cte_1 as
(Select
	oracle_customer_name,
	rev_mth_dt,
	Sum(amount) as revenue
From platinum.txn_normalized
Group by
	oracle_customer_name,
	rev_mth_dt
),
cte_2 as
(
Select
	*,
	Min(rev_mth_dt) over(partition by oracle_customer_name) as m0_month,
	date_trunc('Month', Min(rev_mth_dt) over(partition by oracle_customer_name) + 93)::date as m3_month,
	date_trunc('Month', Min(rev_mth_dt) over(partition by oracle_customer_name) + 186)::date as m6_month,
	date_trunc('Month', Min(rev_mth_dt) over(partition by oracle_customer_name) + 372)::date as m12_month
From cte_1
Group by 
oracle_customer_name,
rev_mth_dt,
revenue
),
cte_3 as
(Select
	row_number() over() as cohort,
	m0_month,
	Count(oracle_customer_name) as cohort_size,
	Sum(revenue) as m0_revenue
From cte_2
Where rev_mth_dt = m0_month
Group by m0_month
Order by m0_month
),
cte_4 as
(Select
	row_number() over() as cohort,
	m0_month,
	Count(oracle_customer_name) as cohort_size,
	Sum(revenue) as m3_revenue
From cte_2
Where rev_mth_dt = m3_month
Group by m0_month
Order by m0_month
),
cte_5 as
(Select
	row_number() over() as cohort,
	m0_month,
	Count(oracle_customer_name) as cohort_size,
	Sum(revenue) as m6_revenue
From cte_2
Where rev_mth_dt = m6_month
Group by m0_month
Order by m0_month
),
cte_6 as
(Select
	row_number() over() as cohort,
	m0_month,
	Count(oracle_customer_name) as cohort_size,
	Sum(revenue) as m12_revenue
From cte_2
Where rev_mth_dt = m12_month
Group by m0_month
Order by m0_month
)
Select
	c3.m0_month as m0_month,
	c3.cohort_size as m0_cohort,
	c4.cohort_size as m3_cohort,
	c5.cohort_size as m6_cohort,
	c6.cohort_size as m12_cohort,
	c3.m0_revenue as m0_revenue,	
	c4.m3_revenue as m3_revenue,	
	c5.m6_revenue as m6_revenue,	
	c6.m12_revenue as m12_revenue
from cte_3 c3
Left join cte_4 c4 on
c3.m0_month = c4.m0_month
Left join cte_5 c5 on
c3.m0_month = c5.m0_month
Left join cte_6 c6 on
c3.m0_month = c6.m0_month


